course: dictionary
lesson: 8775
title: Shadowy and what it tells you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shadowy is a describing word. It can mean full of shadows and dark, or dim and hard to see clearly. «They find the shadowy forest and can smell and hear Giraffe and Zebra but cannot see them at all.» The forest is so dark that the friends can hear and smell their friends but cannot see them.
explain: Shadowy can also describe something faint and not clear, like a figure you can barely make out. Stories often use it for mystery and danger. In The Wind in the Willows the Wild Wood is shadowy and frightening, and the Mole sees faces in the shadows.
explain: To work out which meaning fits, use the context. Ask: is the place dark, is the thing faint, or is the group secret? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Shadowy means full of shadows, dark and hard to see in, as in «a shadowy corner».
fact: Shadowy can mean dim, faint and not clear, as in «a shadowy figure».
fact: Shadowy can also mean mysterious and secret, not well known, as in «a shadowy organisation».
fact: In science, a shadow forms when light is blocked by an object.
fact: Shadowy is an adjective, so it changes to shadowier and shadowiest when you compare things.
exercise: «They find the shadowy forest and can smell and hear Giraffe and Zebra but cannot see them at all.» What does shadowy mean here? | Covered in snow | Bright and sunny, with no places to hide | Very loud and full of music | *Dark and hard to see in
exercise: «The shadowy figure at the gate did not speak.» Which meaning fits best? | Made of wood | Very fast | *Dim, faint and not clear | Bright and cheerful
exercise: A newspaper calls a group a shadowy organisation. What does that suggest? | It meets every morning at the school gate | *Nobody knows much about who is in it or what it does | It is full of happy children | Everyone in it wears a big red hat
test: What is a shadow in science? | A bright light that shines through glass | A kind of cloud | *A dark shape made when light is blocked by an object | A sound that echoes in a cave
test: Which word is the comparative form of shadowy? | shadowyness | *shadowier | shadowing | shadowiest
exam: Which meaning of shadowy fits best in «The shadowy stranger slipped away between the trees.»? | *Dim, faint and hard to make out | Happy and laughing | Loud and shouting | Very tall
